/*****************************************************************************
    cerrT -- the fixture for the `cerr` statement keyword (2026-08-01).

    THE BLOCKER IT CLEARS: genParse's remaining emitters write their PRODUCT via
    cerr and kant had no stderr, so a kant version could not reproduce its own
    target. That is what held minionA round 2. Grammar-minion round 1 refused to
    build it inside its sandbox and named the exact edit (CLAIM GRAM-4); this is
    that edit, made by the foreman, who is allowed to touch shared files.

    THE ORACLE IS THE STREAM SPLIT, not the text. A fixture that only checked
    the text would pass with cerr wired to stdout -- which is precisely the
    defect worth catching. So every row is asserted by running the binary TWICE,
    once with 2>/dev/null and once with 1>/dev/null, and checking that each line
    appears on exactly one stream.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (CLAUDE.md third corollary).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
search reset stack Grokking;
search UnitTests list;
register(CerrTest);
define
    runCerr code={
        print "OUT-1 plain print":;
        cerr  "ERR-1 plain cerr":;
        cerr  "ERR-2 with a value" righty:;
        cerr  #"ERR-3 through a string expression":;
        print "OUT-2 print still works after cerr":;
        };
    ;
runCerr();
print "CT2 SENTINEL":;
stop();
